 852+ B415              ; ================================================================
 853+ B415              ; Extraction services. Both write a byte range into a new file in the
 854+ B415              ; active panel directory; they differ only in where the bytes come from.
 855+ B415              ;
 856+ B415              ; SERVICE_EXTRACT takes them from the loaded data pages, so a plugin can
 857+ B415              ; write back data it has modified in RAM (the editor saves this way).
 858+ B415              ; SERVICE_EXTRACT_SEEK re-reads them from the source file instead, which
 859+ B415              ; is the only way to reach data past the 64KB the viewer keeps in RAM
 860+ B415              ; (TRD disk images are up to 640K).
 861+ B415              ; The shared steps live in view_extract_prepare/open_dest/exit.
 862+ B415              ; ================================================================
 863+ B415
 864+ B415              ; view_extract_prepare: HL=plugin filename, DE=offset bits 0-15,
